# Values scripts/scan-secrets.mjs is allowed to find.
#
# One per line:
#
#     <fingerprint>  why it is allowed
#
# The fingerprint is the first twelve hex characters of the sha256 of the exact
# string that matched. The secret itself is deliberately not written here — a
# file of real credentials with a reassuring name at the top is worse than no
# file at all, and the hash is enough to recognise the same value again.
#
# The scanner prints the fingerprint of anything it stops on, so allowing one is
# a copy and paste of the line it suggests. Say why. A line here is a decision
# somebody made, and in six months the reason is the only part still worth
# having.
#
# This file is tracked, so every addition shows up in a diff and can be argued
# with. For a one-off that does not belong here for good, push once with:
#
#     ALLOW_SECRETS="why this one is fine" git push
#
# which lets it through and writes the reason to the local scan history instead.

